Namazu Elements for Debian and derived distributions
====================================================

The server runs as the `namazu-elements.service` systemd unit (alias:
`elements.service`) under the dedicated `elements` system user.

    systemctl status namazu-elements

Layout:

    /usr/share/namazu-elements/     application (lib/, classpath/)
    /etc/elements/                  elements.properties (operator-owned),
                                    classpath/ (classpath overrides)
    /etc/default/namazu-elements    JVM options (JAVA_OPTS); a conffile
    /var/lib/namazu-elements/       state (cdn-repos, script-repos,
                                    script-storage, tmp)
    /var/log/namazu-elements/       logs (rotated via logrotate)

Configuration precedence: values in /etc/elements/elements.properties take
precedence over environment variables, so keep deployment-specific settings
(Mongo URI, public URLs, bootstrap credentials) in systemd drop-ins under
/etc/systemd/system/namazu-elements.service.d/, using the underscore key
form (e.g. dev_getelements_elements_mongo_uri).

Database migrations run without a container:

    namazu-elements migrate --help

Upgrades preserve /etc/elements and /var/lib/namazu-elements; `apt purge`
removes them only when they are empty.
